    },
    {
      "block_id": 16,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Figure 5-7. Word and Byte Write-Cycle Timing Diagram \n",
      "bbox": [
        136.69000244140625,
        303.2425231933594,
        388.3296203613281,
        316.5703125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.27121032230437747,
        0.4672745822948958,
        0.7704952784946987,
        0.48781173228162056
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 17,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The descriptions of the eight states of a write cycle are as follows: \n",
      "bbox": [
        69.89999389648438,
        327.0125427246094,
        350.3305969238281,
        340.34033203125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13869046408032615,
        0.5039024464566909,
        0.6951003907218812,
        0.5244395964434156
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 18,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 0 \nThe write cycle starts in SO. The processor places valid function codes on \n",
      "bbox": [
        70.06999969482422,
        342.362548828125,
        454.7106018066406,
        355.6903381347656
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13902777717227027,
        0.5275556848439431,
        0.9022035750131758,
        0.5480928348306678
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 19,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "FC2-FCO and drives R/W high (if a preceding write cycle has left R/W low). \n",
      "bbox": [
        127.80999755859375,
        353.40252685546875,
        449.03790283203125,
        366.7303161621094
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.2535912649972098,
        0.54456748472922,
        0.8909482199048239,
        0.5651046347159447
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 20,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 1 \nEntering S1, the processor drives a valid address on the address bus. \n",
      "bbox": [
        70.30999755859375,
        374.29254150390625,
        425.259765625,
        387.6203308105469
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13950396340990823,
        0.5767574716947309,
        0.8437693762400794,
        0.5972946216814556
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 21,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 2 \nOn the rising edge of S2, the processor asserts AS and drives R/W low. \n",
      "bbox": [
        70.30999755859375,
        395.17254638671875,
        433.5007629394531,
        408.5003356933594
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13950396340990823,
        0.6089320343424317,
        0.8601205613878038,
        0.6294691843291564
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 22,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 3 \nDuring S3, the data bus is driven out of the high-impedance state as the \ndata to be written is placed on the bus. \n",
      "bbox": [
        70.30999755859375,
        416.04254150390625,
        456.2278137207031,
        440.4203186035156
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13950396340990823,
        0.6410911726723223,
        0.9052139161125062,
        0.6786555468621341
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 23,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 4 \nAt the rising edge of S4, the processor asserts TIDS, or LOS. The \nprocessor waits for a cycle termination signal (DTACK or SERR) or VPA, an \nM6800 peripheral signal. When VPA is asserted during S4, the cycle \nbecomes a peripheral cycle (refer to Appendix B M6800 Peripheral \nInterface. If neither termination signal is asserted before the falling \nedge at the end of S4, the processor inserts wait states (full clock cycles) \nuntil either DTACK or BERRis asserted. \n",
      "bbox": [
        70.54999542236328,
        446.14501953125,
        457.0166931152344,
        528.2603759765625
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13998014964754618,
        0.6874768929141343,
        0.9067791530064174,
        0.8140106602727226
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 24,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 5 \nDuring SS, no bus signals are altered. \n",
      "bbox": [
        71.02999877929688,
        535.572509765625,
        290.83404541015625,
        548.9003295898438
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14093253726050967,
        0.8252781244330505,
        0.5770516774011036,
        0.8458153214451344
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 25,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "STATE 6 \nDuring S6, no bus signals are altered. \n",
      "bbox": [
        71.02999877929688,
        556.4525146484375,
        290.8024597167969,
        569.7803344726562
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14093253726050967,
        0.8574526870807513,
        0.576989007374597,
        0.8779898840928352
      ]
    },
